{"base_rate":0.34024179620034545,"brier":0.10421381692573402,"bss":0.535749007361735,"bss_hi":0.6148694326292045,"bss_lo":0.44349811092525965,"chart":{"base":[356.1,97.7],"fp":[246.0,275.6],"lead":"62,188.6 272,176.8 482,141.5 692,90.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.54 — higher than 95% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +8pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.7 °C — better than 9% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 97% → rained 88%"},"rel":"65.8,456.5 165.5,374.8 452.4,244.6 671.1,84"},"country":"AD","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.05471502590673577,"ess":320.9049004643979,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Andorra la Vella</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Andorra la Vella rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>98%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 579 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nLA SEU DURGELL, 16.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.54, ranked 10 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(4&ndash;39) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>228</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>52</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>98%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Andorra la Vella</b> <span class=\"muted\">Andorra</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;34% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 34% of days.</p><p>The forecast did far better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.54</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>4&ndash;39\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><